<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Georgy Zhukov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1896">1896</a>–<a href="/years/1974">1974</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Georgy Konstantinovich Zhukov</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Georgy Zhukov was a Soviet military leader and Marshal of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> who served as deputy commander-in-chief of the armed forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-stalin">Joseph Stalin</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">World War II</a>. After fighting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">World War I</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a>, he defeated Japanese forces at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battles-of-khalkhin-gol">Battles of Khalkhin Gol</a> in 1939. Against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> he took part in the actions at Leningrad, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volgograd">Stalingrad</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kursk">Kursk</a>, and in 1945 his 1st Belorussian Front led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a>–Oder Offensive and he oversaw the Soviet victory at the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, after which he accepted the German Instrument of Surrender. Stripped of his positions by Stalin after the war, he became Defence Minister in 1955 but was forced to retire in 1957.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/georgy-zhukov.jpg" alt="Georgy Zhukov" width="330" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: не указан · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Георгий_Константинович_Жуков_в_военной_форме_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
